          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is a thrombophilia or clotting-risk work-up?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "It is a clinician-selected assessment of inherited or acquired influences on thrombosis, not one fixed universal panel. Possible investigations address different mechanisms and may require different specimen or analytical approaches. The actual requested components should match the clinical question; a panel cannot provide a guaranteed prediction of future clots. [H1,H2]"
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "When should I discuss testing after a clot or family-history concern?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Discuss whether a result would change the clinical assessment or decisions. The history, previous event, family context and acquired risk factors matter. Testing is not automatically useful for everyone with a relative who had thrombosis. Timing and possible interference should be planned with the treating clinician. [H2,L1]"
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Do I need fasting or to stop anticoagulants before testing?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Exact fasting, specimen and timing instructions: check with QXL for more information. Give the clinician and laboratory your full medicine list and the date of any clotting event. Anticoagulants and acute illness can affect selected results. Do not stop prescribed anticoagulants or change their schedule for an educational article. [H2]"
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How much does a thrombophilia work-up cost in Bengaluru?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Price: check with QXL for more information. Pricing depends on the requested investigations and collection option. Ask which functional, antibody or genetic studies are included instead of assuming that every “clotting panel” is equivalent. QXL states Same Day reporting; the quotation and arrangements should match the actual clinician-selected request."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Where can I arrange these tests near me in Bengaluru?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "QXL has Kengeri and Yelahanka locations. Eligible home-collection PIN codes, slots and specimen arrangements: check with QXL for more information. Sudden chest pain, breathlessness, collapse or possible stroke symptoms need urgent medical assessment, not a routine thrombophilia appointment. A risk work-up does not diagnose or exclude an acute clot. [H1,H2]"
              }
            }
          ]
